1
00:00:15,306 --> 00:00:18,476
Hey, Pucchi… Did you know?

2
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:22,147
The average number of daily visitors
at the Louvre, Paris in the spring

3
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,482
is about 40,000.

4
00:00:25,108 --> 00:00:27,902
Since its doors opened in 1793,

5
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:30,155
more than 40,000 people flock

6
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:32,991
to view the Mona Lisa
and the Venus de Milo every day.

7
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:36,453
The visitors do not leave
without seeing these two pieces.

8
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,538
Isn't that incredible?

9
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:42,042
Incredible?
Do you mean the number of guests?

10
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,126
That's not it.

11
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,337
Some of the world's
greatest painters and sculptors

12
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:50,091
are able to express their souls
in a form that can be seen by eyes.

13
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:53,762
It's as if they create Stands
that exist beyond time and place.

14
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:55,764
Wouldn't you agree?

15
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:57,682
It's an interesting thought.

16
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:03,563
Does that make Leonardo Da Vinci
and Alexandros of Antioch Stand Users?

17
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:07,692
Yes, but I'm also talking about you.

18
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,694
Your Pale Snake

19
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:12,405
is able to extract and store souls
by giving it form.

20
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,577
Will you betray me one day?

21
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,662
Why do you not attack me?

22
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:21,873
You know that
I would not survive in sunlight

23
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:24,334
and that I lay to rest
in the dark room during the day.

24
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:27,212
All you have to do is
finish me off while I sleep.

25
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:30,131
If you turn my Stand, The World,
into a disc and take it,

26
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:32,300
you yourself could become king.

27
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:34,219
So do it.

28
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:41,351
That has never even crossed my mind.

29
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:45,271
I like people who help me grow.

30
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:47,524
You are the king among kings.

31
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:51,903
I want to follow you
and see what kind of end you will reach.

32
00:01:52,654 --> 00:01:56,241
I love you, in the same manner
as men love their god.

33
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:14,717
Sorry, that wasn't meant to insult you.

34
00:02:15,343 --> 00:02:17,387
It's that I've never considered

35
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:21,141
that there was a man
who could calm my soul just by us talking.

36
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:24,060
I feared losing you.

37
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:27,772
You will become a noble priest.

38
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:30,150
Please, accept this.

39
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,693
It is a symbol of my apology.

40
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:34,571
I extracted it out of my body just now.

41
00:02:35,071 --> 00:02:39,826
No matter where you are, I will always
be able to lend you my powers.

42
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:47,584
EPISODE 22: TIME FOR HEAVEN!
NEW MOON! NEW PRIEST!

43
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:48,626
Jo…

44
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:54,924
Jolyne!

45
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:02,140
Pale Snake.

46
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:06,019
Read Jolyne's whereabouts from that disc.

47
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:08,730
Respond to me.

48
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:11,190
What happened?

49
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:12,358
Is that you there?

50
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,904
Respond to me.

51
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:16,988
Can you not hear me?

52
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:20,491
Why is this transceiver here?

53
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,327
Who is on the other end?

54
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,244
Who?

55
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:25,705
Who the hell is it?

56
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:30,793
All right.

57
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:32,921
I understand.

58
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:35,465
The situation is that serious, huh?

59
00:03:36,174 --> 00:03:37,926
I just left the medical wing.

60
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:39,802
Bastard!

61
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,137
It's Weather Forecast!

62
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:46,059
This rain…

63
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:50,688
Where is the disc?

64
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,276
This bastard!

65
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:58,029
They had Weather Forecast summon rain!

66
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:03,826
You won't escape me!

67
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,622
Damn this rain!

68
00:04:07,705 --> 00:04:10,166
I can't see anything… where did they go?

69
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:15,213
And it's foggy.

70
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:21,761
Where is this sound of
hitting rocks coming from?

71
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:23,263
I think it's Morse Code?

72
00:04:23,846 --> 00:04:25,765
Make the fog thicker…

73
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:27,809
They're after me.

74
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:32,355
Pale Snake's User is Father Pucchi!

75
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:33,648
He knows.

76
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:35,775
He knows who I am!

77
00:04:35,858 --> 00:04:38,319
Weather Forecast knows!

78
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:45,285
Five hundred three.

79
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:47,161
Count the prime numbers.

80
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:48,454
Five hundred nine.

81
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,081
Five hundred twenty-one.

82
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:53,501
Nothing can divide prime numbers.

83
00:04:53,584 --> 00:04:55,795
The reason why people lose…

84
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:57,922
Five hundred twenty-three.

85
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,549
Shame leads men to defeat.

86
00:04:59,632 --> 00:05:01,509
Men die to compensate for their shame.

87
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:03,970
Five hundred forty-one.

88
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:08,516
Thoughts of shameful regret
such as "why did I do that earlier"

89
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:11,019
weakens men
and leads them to their defeat.

90
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:15,189
I didn't make an error by failing
to see the guards' transceiver.

91
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:16,649
No, this is a trial.

92
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:19,485
There are still ways to prevail.

93
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:23,698
Jolyne Cujoh doesn't know who I am yet.

94
00:05:24,282 --> 00:05:26,743
Nothing has changed yet.

95
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:29,203
I haven't completely lost them, either.

96
00:05:29,787 --> 00:05:31,372
True victors…

97
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:34,584
are those who can reign over
the circumstances given to them.

98
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:39,714
It looks like you survived.

99
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:42,925
Weather Forecast.

100
00:05:44,218 --> 00:05:46,095
Where are Jolyne and the others?

101
00:05:48,264 --> 00:05:49,474
Anastasia.

102
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:52,852
I'm really grateful
for everything you've done for me.

103
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:56,064
Thanks to you, I've been safe until now.

104
00:05:56,731 --> 00:05:59,567
But why do you care so much about me?

105
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:04,113
Finding out who Pale Snake is
and getting my father's memory back

106
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:05,698
is my problem, and mine only.

107
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:09,494
Jolyne, how can you say that
when you fully know

108
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:11,537
how I feel towards you?

109
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:14,332
You've already given me so much.

110
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:16,417
I see a bright hope

111
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:19,253
I couldn't find anywhere,
inside or outside of the prison.

112
00:06:19,837 --> 00:06:22,006
And that's why I'm here with you.

113
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:25,468
Hey, what's this?

114
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:26,844
Why is it latching onto me?

115
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:27,887
I'm not sure.

116
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:29,639
"I'm not sure" isn't an answer.

117
00:06:29,722 --> 00:06:31,599
It's chewing on my hair!

118
00:06:36,896 --> 00:06:38,856
It's eating dirt too.

119
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:42,401
So, is it actually a plant?
Does it need nutrients?

120
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,904
But it sleeps a lot too.

121
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:48,783
Jolyne, get down.

122
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:50,201
Something is coming.

123
00:06:56,666 --> 00:07:00,670
There are two of them,
and they've already closed in on us.

124
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:09,720
F.F.!

125
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:13,975
Jolyne… I know who Pale Snake is.

126
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:16,811
It's Father Pucchi, Jolyne.

127
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:20,523
It was Father Pucchi all along.

128
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:22,400
I almost died.

129
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:26,612
If Weather Forecast hadn't come,
I wouldn't be alive right now.

130
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:28,030
F.F.!

131
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:31,409
I'm fine.

132
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:33,202
I only threw out my body.

133
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:36,038
What happened to you guys, Jolyne?

134
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:38,875
Let me heal your right eye.

135
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:41,335
What you said just now…

136
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:45,214
Yes. Father Pucchi
was trying to track down

137
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:47,842
the baby's location from D an' G's memory.

138
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:50,428
Now, we only need to corner him.

139
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:53,473
There's finally a way for us to win.
Weather Forecast came too.

140
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:56,350
Weather Forecast.

141
00:07:56,434 --> 00:07:57,518
Jolyne…

142
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:01,397
Have you recovered from the injuries
you sustained at the factory?

143
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:03,608
Yes. I hope you've been okay.

144
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:12,200
What the hell is this?
What are those two doing?

145
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,618
They are embracing.

146
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:16,454
I know that much! F.F., separate them!

147
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:18,122
Separate them now!

148
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:19,040
I have to do it?

149
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:20,958
Yes, you!

150
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:23,044
Remember our terms?

151
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:25,338
That asshole's smell
is rubbing off on Jolyne!

152
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:28,049
Calm down, it's just a greeting!

153
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:30,301
See? They stopped.

154
00:08:30,384 --> 00:08:31,761
Stop being dramatic.

155
00:08:31,844 --> 00:08:33,596
We found out Pale Snake's identity.

156
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:35,515
We don't have time for this petty fight.

157
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:38,059
Hey, are you talking back to me?

158
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,769
What the hell are you thinking?

159
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:41,979
How dare you forget our promise.

160
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:44,315
You are nothing but plankton.

161
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:48,778
Jolyne, now that we know
who Pale Snake is,

162
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:51,155
we don't need this thing anymore.

163
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:53,491
There's no use for it.

164
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:54,867
Let's kill it.

165
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:57,203
Give me permission, Jolyne.

166
00:08:57,286 --> 00:08:58,204
Wait a minute.

167
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:00,831
It's not your ally, Jolyne.

168
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:02,083
It's not even human.

169
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:04,585
It didn't exist in the first place.

170
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:08,798
This being is lower than animals.
It should have never been born.

171
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:12,301
We shouldn't keep unknown creatures
like this one alive.

172
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:13,678
So please, let me.

173
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:16,138
Now hold on.
You better watch it, Anastasia.

174
00:09:16,222 --> 00:09:19,100
Are you talking about me?
Careful how you phrase things.

175
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:20,893
Don't touch me.

176
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:23,813
We don't have time for that, plankton.

177
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:28,067
Weather Forecast,
you know the situation, right?

178
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:30,403
Give me permission.

179
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:33,239
No. I cannot do that.

180
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,992
You are the one who will die.

181
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:54,885
F.F., who the hell did you bring?

182
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,470
Bastard…

183
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:59,599
Fuck, you got me.

184
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:00,725
This can't be.

185
00:10:00,808 --> 00:10:03,686
This isn't… This can't be happening!

186
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:06,439
He's not Weather Forecast.

187
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:07,565
He's…

188
00:10:07,648 --> 00:10:09,400
He's…

189
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:12,612
We were… being tricked.

190
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:17,783
Thank you, F.F., for taking me here

191
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:23,122
before the real Weather Forecast
caught up.

192
00:10:28,794 --> 00:10:30,963
Five hundred forty-seven.

193
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,840
Five hundred fifty-seven.

194
00:10:32,923 --> 00:10:35,718
No one can divide prime numbers.

195
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:37,637
It took such a long time.

196
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,347
I waited 22 years.

197
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:43,601
The pinnacle of heights
humans are able to achieve…

198
00:10:44,101 --> 00:10:46,479
This is undoubtedly it.

199
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:50,691
We finally meet,
you who will help me get to heaven!

200
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:53,653
Though incomplete and inchoate,

201
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:57,823
the only thing left for me to do is to
trace the memory sealed by Jotaro Kujo.

202
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:00,368
The new moon rises tonight.

203
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:01,494
Dio.

204
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:03,204
No other night is better suited

205
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:06,874
to awaken you once again
so that you benefit my cause.

206
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:11,837
Thirty-six of the worst convicts' souls
were absorbed

207
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:14,173
and gave rise to this new life form.

208
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:17,259
That's what this green creature is.

209
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,637
That reminds me.

210
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,764
Before I begin…

211
00:11:23,557 --> 00:11:28,729
I must send you to an absolute death
where you are forever forgotten.

212
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:32,024
Now stand, Jotaro's daughter.

213
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:33,526
Though I struck a fatal blow,

214
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:36,529
you managed to block
a split second faster than the others.

215
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:42,618
If you won't attack, then I will!

216
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:48,749
I didn't think

217
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:53,087
this was how I'd find out
who you were, Pale Snake.

218
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:56,173
I didn't think
I'd see you again like this.

219
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:58,801
I'm taking three things from you.

220
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:00,761
My father's memory,

221
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:03,305
the disc you took from F.F.,

222
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:06,517
and your life!

223
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:31,208
What is the meaning of these handcuffs?

224
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,051
You've never worn handcuffs before?

225
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:46,182
I had to wear them almost every day
ever since your ploy brought me here.

226
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:49,393
You think you caught me with these?

227
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:51,520
Do you know what handcuffs are for?

228
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:54,607
They aren't to keep someone
from running away.

229
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:57,026
They are used to make others submit!

230
00:12:57,109 --> 00:13:01,697
You still don't seem to understand
what you are doing right now.

231
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:05,701
We are connected through these handcuffs.

232
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:08,913
Do you know what that means?

233
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:12,458
Let's see who is the one
that's being kept here.

234
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:17,838
I already turned your Stone Ocean
into one of my discs.

235
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:21,050
It's so close to falling out,
I can almost grab it.

236
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,511
Do you see it now?

237
00:13:23,594 --> 00:13:28,849
So who is the one in a predicament here,
you or me?

238
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:35,022
Well, I really don't get
what you are on about…

239
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,358
That's all I know.

240
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,026
A few millimeters.

241
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:42,029
A few millimeters, and this fight is over.

242
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:46,784
If I can enter just a few millimeters
within my range of aerial attack,

243
00:13:46,867 --> 00:13:48,369
my fist can land a blow.

244
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:53,582
Some swallows die from flying
directly into cliff walls.

245
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:59,046
It's because their parents
never taught them the safe diving range,

246
00:13:59,129 --> 00:14:01,799
leading the swallows
to soar at a dangerous angle.

247
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:04,843
It's not that the birds' parents
aren't teaching their offspring.

248
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:09,014
The parents cannot teach it because
their own parents never taught them.

249
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:11,934
This family of birds tends to have
a short lifespan,

250
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:15,479
and they don't even realize why
they're prone to dying from accidents.

251
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:18,941
Jotaro had a short lifespan.

252
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:33,622
Stone Ocean is mine!

253
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:42,298
I used her own disc to block her sight…
How did she know where I was?

254
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:45,050
Did she use the cuff's vibrations
to guess?

255
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:51,223
No, it's her strong will!

256
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:55,227
Her strong will detected my attack!

257
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,354
When she first entered prison,

258
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:59,982
I thought she didn't even have
a Stand ability.

259
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:05,195
She seemed like a helpless little girl
crying over some asshole who used her.

260
00:15:06,655 --> 00:15:07,656
This is bad.

261
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:11,118
Her Stone Ocean has an advantage
over my Pale Snake.

262
00:15:11,201 --> 00:15:13,996
At this rate, I'm done for…

263
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:17,374
But more importantly,
the birthed creature will be destroyed!

264
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:23,005
What did you throw just now?

265
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:23,964
What did you do?

266
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:28,928
I'm asking you what you threw!

267
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:33,474
A disc is a physical manifestation
of one's soul.

268
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:35,225
It can be stored forever.

269
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:36,852
However,

270
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:42,775
what if the disc is inserted
into someone on the brink of death?

271
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:48,614
The disc would perish
along with that person's death.

272
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:57,623
That's Jotaro's memory disc
you've risked your life for.

273
00:15:57,706 --> 00:15:59,249
You can have it back.

274
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:03,629
It's stabbed into Anastasia's dying body.

275
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:06,924
What will you do now?
Will you go get the disc?

276
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:09,468
Or will you continue
your handcuff death match?

277
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:15,432
It's risky to let go of Jotaro's disc,

278
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:19,645
but I've already memorized
the contents of the notebook.

279
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,606
All that is left is the execution.

280
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:26,068
What will you choose, Jolyne Cujoh?

281
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:28,946
How can you still be contemplating?

282
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:34,159
Your father is rotting away
along with Anastasia as he wastes away!

283
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:45,462
All that I'm after
is the birthed creature.

284
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,926
I won! As I thought, she chose her father.

285
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:55,097
Spiral staircase, rhinoceros beetle,

286
00:16:55,180 --> 00:17:01,562
city of desolation, fig tart,
rhinoceros beetle, Via Dolorosa,

287
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:05,274
rhinoceros beetle,
singularity point, Giotto,

288
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:10,237
angels, hydrangea, rhinoceros beetle,
singularity point,

289
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,364
secret emperor.

290
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:25,669
You've shown your interest.

291
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:28,672
Are you willing to approach me?

292
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:31,842
Will this be the beginning of everything?

293
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:38,724
Now, I can depart
into your world with you!

294
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:40,976
Hallelujah, Dio!

295
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:44,897
Anastasia!

296
00:17:52,821 --> 00:17:56,200
This can't be happening…

297
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:59,745
No… this can't…

298
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,288
This isn't true!

299
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:03,499
Somebody!

300
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:05,584
Isn't there anyone around here?

301
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:08,962
Somebody! A guard! I'm right here!

302
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:11,757
Please, I need a doctor!

303
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,217
- Hey!
- Diver…

304
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:17,096
- Diver… Drive.
- Please, somebody!

305
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:20,307
- Can you hear me?
- Please, call for help!

306
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:21,600
- F.F…
- Please!

307
00:18:21,683 --> 00:18:25,312
- Help!
- Jolyne is mourning.

308
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:30,567
This is your fault, F.F.

309
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:32,236
Shit…

310
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,696
I'm cold.

311
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:36,698
Actually, I'm freezing.

312
00:18:37,574 --> 00:18:40,536
Looks like my heart's
already stopped beating.

313
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:46,792
I guess her father's memory disc
is inside my body.

314
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:49,795
It will disappear, along with my life.

315
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:55,592
I tried to eject it,
but I'm fighting to stay awake.

316
00:18:56,593 --> 00:18:59,805
Looks like you are crumbling away.

317
00:19:00,389 --> 00:19:02,141
Come claim my everything.

318
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:03,725
You have to be the one to do it.

319
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:06,520
I'll leave my intellect for your use.

320
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:11,483
You can use up all the life
I have left in me too.

321
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:12,985
You can have my body.

322
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:19,241
So come inside my body
and remove the disc for Jolyne.

323
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:22,703
Only you can do it, plankton.

324
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:27,332
Answer me, F.F.

325
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:30,335
We made a deal!

326
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:33,755
You are supposed to follow all my orders.

327
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:36,175
You have to keep your word.

328
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:39,344
You have to stay alive.

329
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:42,306
You can mutate my body as you please.

330
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:44,016
Stop wasting time!

331
00:19:44,099 --> 00:19:45,559
My… consciousness…

332
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:47,644
It's… going…

333
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:53,942
This can't be!

334
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:55,110
Anastasia!

335
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:59,114
No… Jolyne.

336
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,074
It's going to be all right.

337
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:02,826
It's not how it looks.

338
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:04,536
You've done it.

339
00:20:05,412 --> 00:20:06,455
Anastasia…

340
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:09,708
got the disc back for you.

341
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:13,086
F.F., is that you?

342
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:15,047
Are you the one speaking?

343
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:18,342
One thing I feared the most

344
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:23,096
was losing the ability to even think
to say goodbye to my friends.

345
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:25,015
But…

346
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:30,270
in the final moment, I could do just that.

347
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,189
Jolyne,

348
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:35,567
please tell this to Anastasia
once he wakes up.

349
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:38,403
His body belongs to himself.

350
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:42,824
I used his life and intellect
to fill his wounds.

351
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:43,825
Hold on!

352
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:47,579
Why are you talking like this, F.F.?

353
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:50,207
Goodbye, Jolyne.

354
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:53,043
I can't be here any longer.

355
00:20:53,877 --> 00:20:55,712
F.F. is disappearing.

356
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,130
What are you saying?

357
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:58,715
Stop talking like that!

358
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:00,968
Look at me, Jolyne.

359
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,929
This is my soul.

360
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:05,764
This is my intellect.

361
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:09,893
I lived a life.

362
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:13,563
I'll do anything to get your disc back
from the priest.

363
00:21:13,647 --> 00:21:15,732
I'm talking about F.F.'s disc.

364
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:17,442
That will bring you back!

365
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:20,404
That must be a different F.F.

366
00:21:21,863 --> 00:21:23,573
I don't think it would be me.

367
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:25,534
Because this is me.

368
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:28,578
This is me, saying goodbye.

369
00:21:30,455 --> 00:21:34,209
I'm so glad I got to say
my farewells… Jolyne.

370
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:37,045
This is all right, Jolyne.

371
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:39,214
Everything is all right.

372
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:42,884
I'm glad you got your father's disc back.

373
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:49,641
F.F…

374
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:58,900
Respond, F.F.

375
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:01,987
I've lost you, F.F.

376
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:03,613
Where are you?

377
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:05,949
F.F.?

378
00:22:06,783 --> 00:22:08,910
Answer me, F.F.

379
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:12,873
F.F.

380
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:46,383
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
